I have succeded in getting Ularn to compile under Xenix/286. Only a couple
of the source files require the -LARGE option. Since I use CC = cci (posted
some time ago to comp.unix.xenix) I don't remember which ones. 
There is one problem, however. If a spell is cast that projects a beam
(e.g. fire) a segmentation fault occurs. This problem also occured with
NetHack (2.3) and I was able to fix it by compiling some of the modules
huge model (-M2h) and rearranging some of the code that did zapping (zap.c).
I wonder if anyone has a fix for the '286 ? If anyone has would they please
post it to me (or the net). If the fix has not been done would someone
indicate (probably philc@sco.com would be best) if they are interested in
getting a fix. If anyone is I'll do it ASAP otherwise I'll let it slide
for a while.
